Yes! Specialisations: `config.specialisation.<name>` — each specialisation is built as a separate system configuration and gets its own boot entry (e.g., "host-nvidia"). At boot, systemd-boot shows both "host" and "host-nvidia". This is exactly the answer to "same host with a different GPU driver, selectable at boot".

Example:

