{"answer": "Yes. `nixpkgs.lib` is the standard Nix library, and any Nix flake that takes `nixpkgs` as an input — which is the normal setup for a Nix library — can call its functions directly. So a gen library can use `lib.mkOption`, `lib.mkDefault`, `lib.mkOverride`, `lib.types.*`, `lib.assertMsg`, `lib.mapAttrs`, `lib.mkIf`, etc., as long as `nixpkgs` is in its flake inputs (typically `inputs.nixpkgs`), and it references them as `nixpkgs.lib.<fn>` or binds `lib = nixpkgs.lib;`.

